WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.829
Metacognition also appears before the work begins.

2
00:00:02.829 --> 00:00:10.104
Planning means choosing an approach that fits the task instead of automatically using the same strategy every time.

3
00:00:10.104 --> 00:00:12.125
Different tasks require different methods.

4
00:00:12.125 --> 00:00:23.038
Learning a concept, debugging a failure, writing a recommendation, reviewing a design, and preparing for a difficult conversation all place different demands on attention, evidence, and time.

5
00:00:23.038 --> 00:00:25.463
Good planning starts with the outcome.

6
00:00:25.463 --> 00:00:29.504
What are you trying to learn, decide, produce, or improve?

7
00:00:29.504 --> 00:00:31.525
What do you already know?

8
00:00:31.525 --> 00:00:32.738
What is uncertain?

9
00:00:32.738 --> 00:00:34.354
What resources will help?

10
00:00:34.354 --> 00:00:37.588
How difficult is the task likely to be?

11
00:00:37.588 --> 00:00:39.609
Where should you place checkpoints?

12
00:00:39.609 --> 00:00:45.671
These questions help allocate attention and time before momentum carries you into the wrong approach.

13
00:00:45.671 --> 00:00:53.755
Strategy selection includes choosing when to use notes, examples, diagrams, checklists, experiments, retrieval practice, peer review, or a worked example.

14
00:00:53.755 --> 00:00:58.200
A diagram may be the right tool when relationships are confusing.

15
00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:03.050
A checklist may help when steps are repeatable and easy to skip.

16
00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:09.517
A small experiment may be better than another long debate when the issue can be tested.

17
00:01:09.517 --> 00:01:11.942
The practical risk is strategy autopilot.

18
00:01:11.942 --> 00:01:17.600
People often use the method that feels comfortable, not the method the task requires.

19
00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:23.663
A strong metacognitive habit is to pause and ask, what kind of problem is this?

20
00:01:23.663 --> 00:01:25.684
Then choose the strategy deliberately.

21
00:01:25.684 --> 00:01:33.767
That small moment of planning can save hours of effort that would otherwise be spent pushing a mismatched method harder.
